From 7eb711462d9f86c455d86676d7e13279919080ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:17:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(slot): a picked Slot stays inside its edges or face

Two opposite straight edges (or one face / closed ring) picked for a
Slot now bound the room it may cut in. The pick seeds the slot that
fills the room into the endpoints and width, in the pick's own
undoable command (SetOperationGeometry, CreateOperation); generation
and the preview refuse by name, with the numbers, a slot too wide, too
long or placed past the picks (machining2d::SlotBound, world-free, for
the Trochoidal slot too); and a picked Slot is judged against the part
(DepthLaw::Section), so one cut below the picked floor is a Gouge that
holds the post. With nothing picked the typed endpoints rule as before.
The Geometry tab echoes the room or the refusal.

Fixes #1504

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
