From ae0838e5136eadb607e47120a97a9c6a4d11cef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:01:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(slot): pin the fit tolerances and refusals; inscribe
 a chorded face

Review of PR #1522:
- Near-miss pins for FIT_TOL and STRAIGHT_TOL on the edge and the face
  room (0.02 mm out refused, 0.005 mm out taken).
- A pin for every refusal: the face's wall and end laws, the selection
  shapes of slot_bound_of, from_face no area, fit no width, from_edges
  no length, confine's finite/positive guard, and CreateOperation's
  seed with its undo.
- A tessellated round-ended face is inscribed: the fitted slot's radius
  is drawn in by the measured chord sag (up to 5% of the width), never
  the tolerance loosened. A face that still seeds nothing says why in
  the refusal (SlotBound::judge) instead of a bare length refusal.
- face_overshoot is exact: region edges against the slot's centre
  segment (segment distance) plus the end centres' containment, in
  place of 0.5 mm boundary sampling.

Refs #1504

