Subject: [PATCH 5/5] test(slot): pin the face law's segment-crossing branch;
 say the inscribe cap is per side

Review of #1522 (b1e25d27): deleting the crossing branch of
`seg_seg_dist` stayed green - a thin wall across the slot, every
vertex farther than r from the centre line, was accepted. The
reviewer's slit-hole face now pins it ("runs 3.000 mm outside the
picked face"); with the branch removed it goes red.

The INSCRIBE_MAX doc and the decision said a 5% width shrink; the code
caps the draw-in per side (up to 10% of the width). Both now say so.

Refs #1504

